		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3791&amp;p=29583#p29583"><![CDATA[
While I know this is probably not the issue with the firmware.  However, I am wondering if folks experiencing it and solved the problem.<br><br>I am using TYT-MD390UV with BlueDV hotspot enable.  Using my old Samsung Galaxy S8 install BlueDV and TCPUART.  I can transmit with any problem,TX audio quality is great.  But on the RX, the audio was stuttering, breaking up. The audio was bad and hardly understand any QSOs.<br><br>The cellphone in use is connected to the QTH wi-fi, not much chance of a poor network connection.  Both radios I use are fine.  I have used both radios (2 TYT-DM390UV) but instead of BlueDV I tried MMDVM with pi-star installed on my raspberry 3B+, no issue at all.  Audio is good both way TX and the RX.<br><br>There was no audio in or out to be tweaked within BlueDV app unlike the AMBE version.  I am wonder if the radio used for hotspot that connected to the android device have to be setting up properly, like MIC gain or something like that.<br><br>Any help or pointer would be appreciated.<br>73, Kit<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5303">W3KIT</a> — Sat Feb 17, 2024 11:17 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
